diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..fa34e65 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,41 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+The app provides local account registration and authentication through password or
+passkey, plus passkey addition, renaming, removal, and reauthentication at
+`/devtools-times/account`. WebAuthn is implemented with
+[SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/packages/server/). Discoverable
+credentials allow sign-in without entering a username. Both registration and
+sign-in require authenticator user verification.
+
+Run with Node.js 22.13 or later. Configure:
+
+- `AUTH_ORIGIN`: the exact public origin, e.g. `https://news.example.com` (no path
+  or trailing slash). The hostname is the WebAuthn relying party ID. When unset,
+  the request origin is used for local development. Set it explicitly in deployment.
+- `AUTH_DB_PATH`: SQLite database path, default `.data/auth.sqlite`. Deploy on a
+  single Node server with a persistent volume for the database and its WAL files.
+  A horizontally scaled deployment needs a shared database implementation.
+
+Passkeys require HTTPS, with localhost allowed for development. Private keys and
+biometric data never reach the server. The database stores credential public
+keys, counters, metadata, salted scrypt password hashes, and hashed session IDs.
+Session cookies are HttpOnly, SameSite Strict, and Secure on HTTPS. Challenges
+are bound to a browser cookie, expire after five minutes, and are consumed once.
+Management requires identity verification within the last five minutes. Removing
+the last passkey is blocked for accounts without a password.
+
+The former forms called an external Cloud Function. Local accounts are a separate
+authentication store; existing external-service users and password hashes are not
+migrated. Import those accounts through a trusted backend migration before using
+this replacement with existing users. A passkey-only account should add a backup
+passkey: this implementation does not provide account recovery.
+
+Run `pnpm test:auth` for automated API integration tests. These exercise actual
+WebAuthn registration and signed authentication responses using a software
+fixture, plus reauthentication, credential ownership, replay and origin rejection,
+challenge expiry, password fallback, and last-credential protection. No manual
+browser verification is required.
